eless Gardner didn't  give up on his dreams he continued to  seek out investment firms taking odd  jobs to pay the bills in the meantime  dean witter a SAN francisco-based  brokerage firm was interested in Gardner  but refused to bring him on board before  putting them through ten months of  interviews it would be a grueling 10  months Gardner showed up for his first  interview in a t-shirt and dirty jeans  he could have fabricated some  story to explain his appearance instead  Guardian decided to tell the truth in  plain terms Gardner told the interviewer  that his mother of the son had run off  with his child that he was broken and  they've just gotten out of jail the day  before as luck would have it the  interviewer had recently been through a  nasty divorce and could sympathize with  Gardner he was immediately given a  position in the company's training  program in 1987 Gardner launched his own  brokerage firm in Chicago  Gardner rich garden quickly began to  land major clients for his new company  including the pension fund of the  Chicago Teachers Union since then his  business has continued to take off and  Gardner hasn't looked back by not  letting his past hold him back and by  sticking to his vision Chris garden was  able to go from being a homeless man to  being a multi-millionaire to help you  transform your business here are three  action items and you can learn from  Chris Gardner action item number one get  excited about something rule number one  of entrepreneurship is you have to love  what you do you have to have such a  strong passion for it that you'll break  through any barrier jump over any hurdle  to see your vision through it's gonna be  hard and you'll think of giving up  multiple times only your passion for the  business and knowing that you're helping  people will keep you going  Gardner is the first admit that in the  early days of his career his major  motivating force for finding work was  money needed to pay the rent he needed  to be 